# Architecture boundaries

- Rust is production. `server/` is legacy Node retained only as a parity oracle.
- `rust-server/` owns HTTP/WS behavior. Preserve API and golden-fixture compatibility.
- Provider credentials belong only in `satellite/`; core calls keyed APIs over mTLS.
- Keep the satellite provider allowlist strict. Never accept arbitrary upstream hosts.
- Reference data and operational parameters belong in `wr-store`/SQLite, not code.
- `proto/satellite.proto` is authoritative; never hand-edit generated gRPC code.
- Do not commit `.env`, credentials, PKI output, live datasets, or private reports.
- Avoid broad rewrites. This repository has many binaries and parity-sensitive paths.

